WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.002
Harvest at the right time, and handle the roots with care.

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:07.081
Most varieties are ready nine to eighteen months after planting.

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:11.314
Dig up one test plant first, to check the size of the roots.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:15.904
Loosen the soil around the plant, then pull gently from the base of the stem.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:20.922
Avoid cutting or bruising the roots. Damaged roots spoil faster.

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:27.288
Fresh roots spoil within two to three days. Harvest only what you can sell or process quickly.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:36.083
Before you move on, check: Dig a test plant first. Loosen soil before pulling. Harvest only what you can use.

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:39.864
In the next lesson: Handling and processing.
